+POOLS, 2026-10-13 (remediation F4). A lot pools its LEARNING, VALIDATION and
+HOLDOUT questions, so a bias confined to one pool is diluted by the others. The
+holdout showed it: 34 of its 64 single-answer questions with a strictly longest
+choice had the correct one longest (53%), while no lot failed. Each exam pool is
+now also measured as its own group, `pool/LEARNING`, `pool/VALIDATION`,
+`pool/HOLDOUT`, with the same test and alpha. The holdout is the bank that is
+meant to measure the candidate, so it is the last one that may be gamed by
+length. Only aggregate counts are printed for it, never a question.
+
+Exit code 1 if any lot's or pool's excess is beyond chance at alpha.
 
